{
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "tool",
      "name": "quote",
      "output_key": "quote",
      "tool": "market_quote",
      "args": {
        "ticker": "{{question}}"
      },
      "fail_ok": true
    },
    {
      "type": "tool",
      "name": "path",
      "output_key": "path",
      "tool": "candlesticks",
      "args": {
        "ticker": "{{question}}",
        "hours_back": 0.25,
        "hourly": false
      },
      "fail_ok": true
    },
    {
      "type": "tool",
      "name": "tape",
      "output_key": "tape",
      "tool": "previous_trades",
      "args": {
        "ticker": "{{question}}",
        "limit": 30
      },
      "fail_ok": true
    },
    {
      "type": "prompt",
      "name": "detect_absorption",
      "output_key": "absorption",
      "prompt": "Contract: {{question}}\nGame: {{game}}\nQuote: {{quote}}\nLast 15 min bars: {{path}}\nRecent trades: {{tape}}\n\nDetect if the market is STILL ABSORBING a recent goal or major event:\n\n1. Look at the minute bars - was there a jump of 10+ cents in the LAST 1-3 MINUTES?\n2. Check if game.recent_events shows a goal in the last 1-5 minutes.\n3. If yes to either: the market may still be moving in that direction (continuation) for another 2-5 minutes.\n4. If the jump was 5+ minutes ago, it's fully absorbed - no continuation expected.\n\nBe precise about timestamps. A goal at minute 17 when we're at minute 20 is 3 minutes old.\n\nKey insight: Goals cause 15-30 cent moves that take 2-4 minutes to fully absorb. If we're in that window, predict continuation. If not, predict zero.",
      "tools": [],
      "max_tool_iterations": 0,
      "output_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "recent_goal_or_jump": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "description": "True if there was a goal in the last 5 minutes OR a 10+ cent price jump in the last 3 minutes"
          },
          "minutes_since_event": {
            "type": "number",
            "description": "How many minutes ago was the goal or jump? null if none."
          },
          "jump_direction": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": ["up", "down", "none"],
            "description": "Direction of the recent jump if any"
          },
          "magnitude_cents": {
            "type": "number",
            "description": "Size of the jump in cents, 0 if none"
          },
          "still_absorbing": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "description": "True if the event was less than 3 minutes ago and the market likely hasn't finished moving"
          },
          "current_mid_cents": {
            "type": "number"
          },
          "three_minutes_ago_cents": {
            "type": "number",
            "description": "Mid price 3 minutes ago"
          }
        },
        "required": ["recent_goal_or_jump", "minutes_since_event", "jump_direction", "magnitude_cents", "still_absorbing", "current_mid_cents", "three_minutes_ago_cents"]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "prompt",
      "name": "predict",
      "output_key": "prediction",
      "prompt": "Contract: {{question}}\nGame: {{game}}\nQuote: {{quote}}\nAbsorption analysis: {{absorption}}\n\nForecast the next 5 minutes using these rules:\n\n**DEFAULT TO ZERO**: Most 5-minute windows have no meaningful price movement. Only predict non-zero if one of these applies:\n\n1. **Still absorbing a recent goal** ({{absorption.still_absorbing}} = true): If a goal/major event happened less than 3 minutes ago and the price jumped {{absorption.magnitude_cents}} cents, it may continue another 20-40% of that move in the same direction. Predict continuation.\n\n2. **Thin book mean reversion**: If the spread is 2+ cents and the price just jumped 3+ cents in the last 1-2 minutes (but no goal in game state), it was likely a single order moving a thin book. Predict 50% retracement.\n\n3. **Very late game time decay** (85+ minutes): If one team leads and clock is 85'+, predict 0.5-1.0 cents per 5 minutes in favor of the leader. But ONLY at 85+, not at 60' or 70'.\n\nIf NONE of these apply, predict delta_cents = 0.\n\n**Calibration**:\n- Typical goal causes 20 cent jump over 3-4 minutes (5-7 cents per minute initially, slowing down)\n- At 2 minutes post-goal: predict 2-4 cents continuation\n- At 5+ minutes post-goal: predict 0 cents\n- Time decay before 80': essentially zero, maybe 0.2 cents per 5 min\n- Time decay 80-85': 0.5 cents per 5 min for leading team\n- Time decay 85'+: 1-1.5 cents per 5 min for leading team\n\n**Half-width**: \n- Use current spread as baseline (quote.spread * 100 cents)\n- Add 1-2 cents for your forecast uncertainty\n- Tighter (1.5-2 cents) when predicting zero on a stable liquid book\n- Wider (3-4 cents) when predicting non-zero or book is thin\n\nOutput delta_cents (the CHANGE in mid, negative for down), half_width_cents, confidence, driver, falsifier.",
      "tools": [],
      "max_tool_iterations": 0,
      "output_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "delta_cents": {
            "type": "number",
            "description": "How many cents the mid will MOVE over the next five minutes. Negative for down, 0 for no move (the most common answer). This is the CHANGE, not the price level."
          },
          "half_width_cents": {
            "type": "number",
            "description": "Half the width of the tightest two-sided market you would stand behind, in cents. Typically current spread plus 1-2 cents for uncertainty."
          },
          "confidence": {
            "type": "number",
            "description": "0-1. How sure you are."
          },
          "driver": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The primary reason: 'still absorbing recent goal', 'thin book reversion', 'late-game time decay', or 'stable/no catalyst'."
          },
          "falsifier": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "What would prove this wrong within 5 minutes."
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "delta_cents",
          "half_width_cents",
          "confidence",
          "driver",
          "falsifier"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    }
  ]
}

{
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "tool",
      "name": "quote",
      "output_key": "quote",
      "tool": "market_quote",
      "args": {
        "ticker": "{{question}}"
      },
      "fail_ok": true
    },
    {
      "type": "tool",
      "name": "path",
      "output_key": "path",
      "tool": "candlesticks",
      "args": {
        "ticker": "{{question}}",
        "hours_back": 1.0,
        "hourly": false
      },
      "fail_ok": true
    },
    {
      "type": "tool",
      "name": "tape",
      "output_key": "tape",
      "tool": "previous_trades",
      "args": {
        "ticker": "{{question}}",
        "limit": 20
      },
      "fail_ok": true
    },
    {
      "type": "prompt",
      "name": "analyze",
      "output_key": "analysis",
      "prompt": "Contract: {{question}}\nGame state: {{game}}\nCurrent book: {{quote}}\nMinute bars (last 60min): {{path}}\nRecent prints: {{tape}}\n\nAnalyze the market state:\n\n1. RECENT EVENT ABSORPTION: Look at recent_events. If a goal/card happened in the last 1-3 minutes, compare current mid to the candlestick history. Has the price already spiked and stabilized? Or is it still moving?\n\n2. TIME DECAY DIRECTION: \n   - If a team is WINNING: their win probability INCREASES as time passes without the other team scoring. Their price should drift UP.\n   - If a team is LOSING: their win probability DECREASES as time passes. Their price should drift DOWN.\n   - If DRAWING: both win probabilities decrease; the draw becomes more likely.\n   \n3. MAGNITUDE: Goals that just happened (0-2 min ago) can cause 10-20 cent moves as they're absorbed. Time decay in stable situations is typically 0-2 cents per 5 minutes.\n\n4. BOOK QUALITY: Wide spread or thin tape means less confidence.\n\nProvide structured analysis of these factors.",
      "tools": [],
      "max_tool_iterations": 0,
      "output_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "event_status": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "absorbed|absorbing|stable - whether recent events are already priced in"
          },
          "time_decay_direction": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "up|down|neutral - which way time passing should move this contract"
          },
          "expected_magnitude": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "large|medium|small - expected size of move based on situation"
          },
          "reasoning": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Why you assess it this way"
          }
        },
        "required": ["event_status", "time_decay_direction", "expected_magnitude", "reasoning"]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "prompt",
      "name": "predict",
      "output_key": "prediction",
      "prompt": "Based on your analysis: {{analysis}}\n\nGiven:\n- Current mid: {{quote.mid}}\n- Game: {{game}}\n- Event status: {{analysis.event_status}}\n- Time decay direction: {{analysis.time_decay_direction}}\n- Expected magnitude: {{analysis.expected_magnitude}}\n\nPredict the move over the next 5 minutes:\n\n- If event_status is 'absorbed' and situation is stable: predict small moves (0-2 cents) in the time_decay_direction\n- If event_status is 'absorbing': predict continued medium moves (3-8 cents) in the direction the price has been trending\n- If expected_magnitude is 'large': be bold with 8-15 cent predictions when warranted\n- If the book is wide (spread > 2 cents) or thin: increase half_width_cents to reflect uncertainty\n\nIMPORTANT: \n- Zero cents is valid for truly stable situations\n- Time decay for a WINNING team means price goes UP\n- Time decay for a LOSING team means price goes DOWN\n- Recent goals (< 3 min) often cause continued drift as the book adjusts\n- Early in matches (< 15'), volatility is higher",
      "tools": [],
      "max_tool_iterations": 0,
      "output_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "delta_cents": {
            "type": "number",
            "description": "How many cents the mid will MOVE over the next five minutes. Negative for down, 0 for no move. This is the CHANGE, not a price level."
          },
          "half_width_cents": {
            "type": "number",
            "description": "Half the width of the tightest two-sided market you would stand behind. Wider when uncertain or thin book."
          },
          "confidence": {
            "type": "number",
            "description": "0-1. How sure you are given book quality and situation clarity."
